1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,846
Hello, you two. Yes, both of you, grown up as well.

2
00:00:05,846 --> 00:00:10,608
And Bloop, who has lost a jigsaw piece again.

3
00:00:11,408 --> 00:00:16,775
By the end of this, you'll spot a trick that works on grown ups every day.

4
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:24,159
Three slow breaths, out longer than in. Breathe in for four.

5
00:00:24,159 --> 00:00:26,874
And out for six. Once more.

6
00:00:26,874 --> 00:00:34,316
This is a spotting job, and a fast brain walks straight past small things.

7
00:00:35,666 --> 00:00:37,976
Today's word is jigsaw.

8
00:00:37,976 --> 00:00:42,095
Small pieces that join up into a picture.

9
00:00:42,095 --> 00:00:45,310
And tonight, the picture is you.

10
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:52,660
Here's how it works. Monday. A game ends, and a box pops up:

11
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:57,560
put your real name on the leaderboard. So you do.

12
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:05,182
Tuesday. A quiz. What animal are you? Pop in your birthday.

13
00:01:05,182 --> 00:01:05,820
Otter.

14
00:01:07,169 --> 00:01:08,213
Wednesday.

15
00:01:08,213 --> 00:01:13,951
Someone in your team chat, nice to you for weeks, asks:

16
00:01:13,951 --> 00:01:19,375
which school do you go to? My cousin might be there.

17
00:01:19,375 --> 00:01:25,322
And you nearly answer, because it would feel rude not to.

18
00:01:26,672 --> 00:01:32,115
Three little things, and not one of them felt like anything.

19
00:01:32,115 --> 00:01:33,929
Now watch them join.

20
00:01:34,729 --> 00:01:37,854
Your name. Your birthday. Your school.

21
00:01:37,854 --> 00:01:45,915
That's enough to answer the little questions when someone taps forgot my password on your account.

22
00:01:45,915 --> 00:01:49,451
Somebody walking in through the front door.

23
00:01:50,801 --> 00:01:56,038
Here's the bit to keep. Nobody asks for all three at once.

24
00:01:56,038 --> 00:01:58,566
You'd spot it straight away.

25
00:01:59,366 --> 00:02:07,502
So it comes one piece at a time, on different days, and every piece feels like nothing.

26
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:10,589
That isn't you missing something.

27
00:02:10,589 --> 00:02:14,517
That's the trick, working as it was built.

28
00:02:14,517 --> 00:02:18,632
And a trick you can see has stopped working.

29
00:02:19,982 --> 00:02:25,825
Pause me here. Grown up, ask the question on the screen.

30
00:02:25,825 --> 00:02:26,868
I'll wait.

31
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:35,661
So how do you catch a piece? Three questions.

32
00:02:35,661 --> 00:02:41,549
Could this help somebody find me? Get into something of mine?

33
00:02:41,549 --> 00:02:47,147
Pretend to be me? If even one answer is yes, it's a piece.

34
00:02:47,147 --> 00:02:51,297
And pieces stay on your side of the screen.

35
00:02:52,647 --> 00:02:59,206
Six things are always a yes, so you don't even need the test.

36
00:02:59,206 --> 00:03:04,797
Full name. School. Address. Phone number. Passwords.

37
00:03:04,797 --> 00:03:09,635
Any photo that shows where you live or learn.

38
00:03:10,435 --> 00:03:15,659
Sometimes they do have to go in somewhere, like a school account.

39
00:03:15,659 --> 00:03:19,918
That's fine, because a grown up is doing it with you.

40
00:03:19,918 --> 00:03:22,088
On your own, they stay out.

41
00:03:23,438 --> 00:03:27,104
A piece hardly ever looks like a question.

42
00:03:27,104 --> 00:03:32,255
It comes wrapped in something good. Free coins. A fun quiz.

43
00:03:32,255 --> 00:03:34,961
Somebody being really friendly.

44
00:03:34,961 --> 00:03:41,333
When something lovely turns up with a box underneath, that's your moment.

45
00:03:42,683 --> 00:03:48,858
And there's one move to know by name. Someone from a game says:

46
00:03:48,858 --> 00:03:53,661
let's chat somewhere else. Or: don't tell anyone.

47
00:03:54,461 --> 00:03:59,409
That's always a check with your grown up moment. Every time.

48
00:03:59,409 --> 00:04:01,719
Even if they've been lovely.

49
00:04:03,069 --> 00:04:08,106
You're not being rude, and you're not deciding alone.

50
00:04:08,106 --> 00:04:10,197
In a chat you can say:

51
00:04:10,197 --> 00:04:16,279
nah, not that one, what's your best score? A box, you just shut.

52
00:04:16,279 --> 00:04:19,796
Then you mention it to your grown up.

53
00:04:19,796 --> 00:04:23,502
That's checking, not telling on anyone.

54
00:04:24,852 --> 00:04:26,353
Pause me again.

55
00:04:26,353 --> 00:04:31,455
Grown up, say a few things out loud, one at a time.

56
00:04:31,455 --> 00:04:33,656
Piece, or not a piece?

57
00:04:38,106 --> 00:04:42,206
Out loud, both of you. Grown up first.

58
00:04:42,206 --> 00:04:45,874
One piece is never just one piece!

59
00:04:46,674 --> 00:04:51,703
Again, together. One piece is never just one piece!

60
00:04:52,503 --> 00:04:58,641
Last one, properly loud. One piece is never just one piece!

61
00:04:59,991 --> 00:05:02,784
Tonight, play Five Pieces.

62
00:05:02,784 --> 00:05:07,833
Your grown up asks you five friendly questions.

63
00:05:07,833 --> 00:05:11,700
Some are pieces, some are just nice.

64
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:15,352
A point for every piece you catch.

65
00:05:16,152 --> 00:05:20,146
Then swap, and see if you can catch them out.

66
00:05:20,146 --> 00:05:24,938
Grown ups, let yourself get caught. It's the best bit.

67
00:05:26,288 --> 00:05:29,339
One last thing, and it matters most.

68
00:05:29,339 --> 00:05:35,609
If you're thinking, I've already put some of that in somewhere, then good.

69
00:05:35,609 --> 00:05:40,354
Go and tell a grown up you trust. Tonight, or next week.

70
00:05:41,154 --> 00:05:49,239
Usually that's the person sitting next to you. A teacher counts.

71
00:05:49,239 --> 00:05:52,524
A nan or an auntie counts.

72
00:05:52,524 --> 00:05:58,336
And Childline is free, on 0800 1111, any time.

73
00:05:59,136 --> 00:06:04,793
Nothing is ruined. Some of it you change, some you take down.

74
00:06:04,793 --> 00:06:09,524
And you will never, ever be in trouble for telling.

75
00:06:10,874 --> 00:06:16,442
Oh, Bloop. There it was. One piece is never just one piece.

76
00:06:17,242 --> 00:06:21,401
Goodbye from DiGi. See you next time.
